{
  "title": "68: al-Qalam القلم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM.\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nنٓ وَٱلْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ (1)\nNAA WALQALAME WA MAA YASTUROONA.\nNun’ and (N) by the Pen and by what they write\nمَآ أَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ (2)\nMAA AANTA BE-NE’MATE RABBEKA BEMAJNOONIN.\nThou (O’ Our Prophet!) by the grace of thy Lord, art not mad\nوَإِنَّ لَكَ لَأَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ (3)\nWA INNA LAKA LAAAJRAN GHAYRA MAMNOONIN.\nAnd verily there is for thee a recompense unending (unobliging)\nوَإِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ (4)\nWAEENNAKA LAA’ALAA KHULUQIN A’AZEEMIN.\nAnd most certainly thou standest on sublime morality\nفَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ (5)\nFASATUBSERU WAYUBSEROONA.\nSo thou wilt see and they (too) wilt see\nبِأَييِّكُمُ ٱلْمَفْتُونُ (6)\nBEAAYYYEKUMU LMAFTOONU.\nWhich of you is demented\nإِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ أَعْلَمُ بِٱلْمُهْتَدِينَ (7)\nINNA RABBAKA HOWA AAA’LAMU BEMAN ZALLA A’AN SABEELEHE WA HOWA AAA’LAMU BELMUHTADEENA.\nVerily thy Lord! He knoweth best of him who is astray from His way, and He knoweth best of those guided aright\nفَلَا تُطِعِ ٱلْمُكَذِّبِينَ (8)\nFALAA LAA LMUKAZZEBEENA.\nSo yield thou not to the beliers!\nوَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ (9)\nWADDOOA LAW TUDHENU FAYUDHENOONA.\nWish they that thou shouldst be pliant so they (too) would be pliant\nوَلَا تُطِعْ كُلَّ حَلَّافٍ مَّهِينٍ (10)\nWA LAA TO-TE’ KULLA HALLAAFIN MMAHEENIN.\nAnd yield thou not unto any despicable swearer\nهَمَّازٍ مَّشَّآءٍۭ بِنَمِيمٍ (11)\nHAMMAAZIN MMASSHAAIN BENAMEEMIN.\nDefamer, going about with slander\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ أَثِيمٍ (12)\nMMANNAAA’IN LLELKHAYRE MO’TADIN AASEEMIN.\nVehement hinderer of good, uncontrolled transgressor, sunk deep in sin\nعُتُلٍّۭ بَعْدَ ذَٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ (13)\nU’UTULLIN BA’DA ZAALEKA ZANEEMIN.\nCruelly violent, besides all that, baseborn\nأَن كَانَ ذَا مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ (14)\nAAN KAANA ZAL MAALIN WABANEENA.\nJust because possesses he wealth and sons\nإِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ ءَايَٰتُنَا قَالَ أَسَٰطِيرُ ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ (15)\nEEZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATUNAA QAALA AASAATEERU LAAWLEENA.\nWhen unto him are recited Our signs, sayeth he: (they are the) “Stories of yore” (legends of the ancients)\nسَنَسِمُهُۥ عَلَى ٱلْخُرْطُومِ (16)\nSANASEMUHU A’LAL LKHURTOOME.\nWe will brand him on the snout!\nإِنَّا بَلَوْنَٰهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَآ أَصْحَٰبَ ٱلْجَنَّةِ إِذْ أَقْسَمُوا۟ لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ (17)\nEENNAA BALAWNAAHUM KAMAA BALAWNAA AASHAABA LJANNATE EEZ AAQSAMOOA LAYASREMUNNAHAA MUSBEHEENA.\nVerily We will try them as We did try the owners of the garden, when they vowed that they would certainly pluck the fruits at morn\nوَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ (18)\nWA LAA YASTASNOONA.\nAnd made no (room for) exception (for the will of God) (saying ‘If God willeth it’)\nفَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَآئِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَآئِمُونَ (19)\nFATAAFA A’LAYHAA TAAEFUN MMEN RABBEKA WA HUM NAAEMOONA.\nSo encircled it a visitation from thy Lord, (rendering the garden desolate) while they were asleep\nفَأَصْبَحَتْ كَٱلصَّرِيمِ (20)\nFAAASBAHAT KALSSAREEME.\nAnd it became like black barren soil\nفَتَنَادَوْا۟ مُصْبِحِينَ (21)\nFATANAADAWA MUSBEHEENA.\nAnd they cried out one unto each other at morn\nأَنِ ٱغْدُوا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَٰرِمِينَ (22)\nAANE GHDOOA A’LAA HARSEKUM EEN KUNTUM SAAREMEENA.\nBe ye early at your tilth if ye would pluck (the fruits)\nفَٱنطَلَقُوا۟ وَهُمْ يَتَخَٰفَتُونَ (23)\nFANTALAQOOA WA HUM YATAKHAAFATOONA.\nAnd went they whispering unto each other\nأَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا ٱلْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ (24)\nAAN LAA YADKHULANNAHAA LYAWMA A’ALAYKUM MMESKEENUN.\nSaying: “No poor man shall enter it today upon you\nوَغَدَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قَٰدِرِينَ (25)\nWAGHADAWA A’LAA HARDIN QAADEREENA.\nAnd at morn went they, strong in their resolve (to prevent the poor)\nفَلَمَّا رَأَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ إِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ (26)\nFALAMMAA RAAAWHAA QAALOOA EENNAA LAZAALLOONA.\nBut when they beheld it, said they: “Verily we have strayed!\nبَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ (27)\nBAL NAHNO MAHROOMOONA.\nNay! we are (the) deprived ones (of the fruits of our labour).\nقَالَ أَوْسَطُهُمْ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ (28)\nQAALA AAWSATUHUM AALAM AAQUL LAKUM LAWLAA TUSABBEHOONA.\nSaid the most balanced one of them: “Said I not unto you, ‘Why should ye not glorify (God)’?\nقَالُوا۟ سُبْحَٰنَ رَبِّنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَٰلِمِينَ (29)\nQAALUD SUBHAANA RABBENAA EENNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEENA.\nSaid they: “Hallowed be Our Lord! Verily we have been unjust!\nفَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلَٰوَمُونَ (30)\nFAAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YATALAAWAMOONA.\nThen some of them proceeded against the others, reproaching each other\nقَالُوا۟ يَٰوَيْلَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا طَٰغِينَ (31)\nQAALUD YAAWAYLANAA EENNAA KUNNAA TAAGHEENA.\nSaid they: “O’ woe unto us! Verily we have been arrogant!\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّنَآ أَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَآ إِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رَٰغِبُونَ (32)\nA’ASAA RABBUNAA AAN YUBDELANAA KHAYRAN MMENHAA INNAA EELAA RABBENAA RAAGHEBOONA.\nHapply, our Lord will give us in exchange a better one than it; Verily unto our Lord do we turn (in repentance)\nكَذَٰلِكَ ٱلْعَذَابُ وَلَعَذَابُ ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ أَكْبَرُ لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ (33)\nKAZAALEKA LA’AZAABU LA-A’ZAABUL LAAKHERATE AAKBARU LAW KAANOOA YAA’LAMOONA.\nSuch hath been Our chastisement, and certainly the chastisement of the hereafter is greater still; Did they but know (it)!\nإِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ (34)\nINNA LIL-MUTTAQEENA E’ENDA RABBEHIM JANNAATE LNNAE’EEME.\nVerily, for the pious ones with their Lord are the Gardens of bliss\nأَفَنَجْعَلُ ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ كَٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ (35)\nAAFANAJA’ALU LMUSLEMEENA KALMUJREMEENA.\nWhat! shall We then make the ‘Muslims’ like unto the guilty ones?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ (36)\nMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKUMOONA.\nWhat is the matter with you? How judge ye\nأَمْ لَكُمْ كِتَٰبٌ فِيهِ تَدْرُسُونَ (37)\nAAM LAKUM KETAABUN FEEHE TADRUSOONA.\nOr have ye a scripture wherein ye read?\nإِنَّ لَكُمْ فِيهِ لَمَا تَخَيَّرُونَ (38)\nINNA LAKUM FEEHE LAMAA TAKHAYROONA.\nVerily, therein is for you what ye choose?\nأَمْ لَكُمْ أَيْمَٰنٌ عَلَيْنَا بَٰلِغَةٌ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ إِنَّ لَكُمْ لَمَا تَحْكُمُونَ (39)\nAAM LAKUM AAYMAANUN A’LAYNAA BAALEGHATUN EELAA YAWMIL LQEEMATE INNA LAKUM LAMAA TAHKUMOONA.\nOr have ye a sworn covenant from Us tending to the Day of Judgment that ye shall surely have whatever ye judge?\nسَلْهُمْ أَيُّهُم بِذَٰلِكَ زَعِيمٌ (40)\nSALHUM AAYHUM BEZAALEKA ZAE’EEMUN.\nAsk them (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) which of them will guarantee that!\nأَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فَلْيَأْتُوا۟ بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ إِن كَانُوا۟ صَٰدِقِينَ (41)\nAAM LAHUM SHURAKAAU FALYAATOOA BE-SHORAKAAA-EHIM EEN KAANOOA SAADEQEENA.\nOr have they any ‘Partners’ (to Us)? Then let them bring their partners (associate gods) if they be truthful!\nيَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَن سَاقٍ وَيُدْعَوْنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ (42)\nYAWMA YUKSHAFU A’AN SAAQIN WAYUDA’AWNA EELAA LSSUJOODE FALAA YASTATEEU’OONA.\nOn the Day that the shin shall be laid bare, (i.e. befalleth an affliction), and they shall be called upon to prostrate in obeisance, but they shall not be able (to do it)\nخَٰشِعَةً أَبْصَٰرُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ وَقَدْ كَانُوا۟ يُدْعَوْنَ إِلَى ٱلسُّجُودِ وَهُمْ سَٰلِمُونَ (43)\nKHAASHEA’ATAN AABSAARUHUM TARHAQUHUM ZELLATUN WA QAD KAANOOA YUDA’AWNA EELAA LSSUJOODE WA HUM SAALEMOONA.\nCasting down their looks, shall cover them abasement, and indeed they had been called upon to prostrate in obeisance, while yet they were whole (healthy)\nفَذَرْنِى وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهَٰذَا ٱلْحَدِيثِ سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ (44)\nFAZARNEAA WAMAN YOKAZZEBO BEHAAZAA LHADEESE SANASTADREJUHUM MIN HAYSO LAA YAA’LAMOONA.\nSo leave Me and him who belieth this announcement, We will lead them on (to ruin) by steps from whence they know not\nوَأُمْلِى لَهُمْ إِنَّ كَيْدِى مَتِينٌ (45)\nWAAUMLEAA LAHUM INNA KAYDEAA MATEENUN.\nAnd yet respite them; for verily My device is firm\nأَمْ تَسَْٔلُهُمْ أَجْرًا فَهُم مِّن مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُونَ (46)\nAAM TASLUHUM AAJRAN FAHUM MMEN MMAGHRAMIN MMUSQALOONA.\nOr askest thou from them a recompense that they are burdened with a load of debt?\nأَمْ عِندَهُمُ ٱلْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ (47)\nAAM E’ENDAHUMU LGHAYBU FAHUM YAKTUBOONA.\nOr with them is the knowledge of the unseen, that they write (it) down?\nفَٱصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ ٱلْحُوتِ إِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ (48)\nFASBER LE HUKME RABBEKA WA LAA TAKUN KASAAHEBE LHOOTE EEZ NAADAA WA HOWA MAKZOOMUN.\nSo wait thou patiently for the judgment of thy Lord! Be not thou like unto the Companion of the fish! when cried he when he was confined\nلَّوْلَآ أَن تَدَٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِٱلْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ (49)\nLLAWLAA AAN TADAARAKAHU NEA’MATUN MMEN RRABBEHE LANUBEZA BELA’ARAAE WA HOWA MAZMOOMUN.\nHad not a bounty from his Lord reached him, he would certainly have been cast forth on the naked shore while in disgrace\nفَٱجْتَبَٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَجَعَلَهُۥ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ (50)\nFAJTABAAHU RABBUHU FAJAA’ALAHU MENAL LSSAALEHEENA.\nThen chose him his Lord and made him of the righteous ones\nوَإِن يَكَادُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ بِأَبْصَٰرِهِمْ لَمَّا سَمِعُوا۟ ٱلذِّكْرَ وَيَقُولُونَ إِنَّهُۥ لَمَجْنُونٌ (51)\nWAEEN YAKAADUL LLAZEENA KAFARUL LAYUZLEQOONAKA BEAABSAAREHEM LAMMAA SAME-O’L LZZEKRA WAYAQOOLOONA EENNAHU LAMAJNOONUN.\nAnd those who disbelieve would almost smite thee with their eyes when they hear the Reminder, and say they: “Verily he is mad\nوَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ (52)\nWA MAA HOWA EELLAA ZIKRUNW LLELA’AALAMEENA.\nAnd it is naught but a Reminder unto the worlds (the whole Mankind)",
